n fails because `cgFile.cpp` actually depends on the `cgio_*` functions from `<cgns_io.h>`. I need to check what `cgFile.cpp` is actually using from that header - is it just the low-level C functions, or is it somehow pulling in the C++ wrapper?\n\nIf it only needs the `cgio_*` C functions, I could keep the include but still remove the cgio library linkage. The `cgio_*` functions come from libcgns.so anyway, not from the internal cgio project.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I see the complexity now. The `cgFile.cpp` actually uses the `cgio_*` C functions from CGNS library's `<cgns_io.h>`, not the internal C++ cgio library. Let me analyze what's needed:\n\n- CGNS library (`libcgns.so`) provides `cgio_*` C functions (low-level)\n- Internal `cgio` project provides `CGIO::*` C++ classes (high-level wrapper)\n- The symbol conflict might be happening because both libraries are linked\n\nLet me check if we can keep `<cgns_io.h>` but remove the internal cgio linkage:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-512ddad1976d4f5185264d668f35e795","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/cgnsMeshCutter/src/cgFile.cpp","newText":"#include \"cgFile.h\"\n#include \"format.h\"\n\n#include <cgns_io.h>\n\n#include <algorithm>","oldText":"#include \"cgFile.h\"\n#include \"format.h\"\n\n#include <algorithm>"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-40310351eb28463f9d274e267c1a0fe6","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/cgnsMeshCutter/src/metisCutter.cpp","newText":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <ctime>\n#include <numeric>\n\n#include <cgns_io.h>\n#include <parmetis.h>","oldText":"#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <ctime>\n#include <numeric>\n\n#include <parmetis.h>"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1436,"cacheRead":21954,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23392,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"ca